# Cloudflare applies these headers to every route. Mirrors the NCS portfolio pattern.
# Content-Security-Policy beyond frame-ancestors is intentionally not set — getting it right
# requires testing because of the Sanity CDN, Web3Forms POST, Calendly iframe, and the
# Cloudflare Analytics beacon. Revisit post-launch.
#
# frame-ancestors: replaces the legacy X-Frame-Options so a Studio can iframe this
# site for preview. Modern browsers prefer CSP frame-ancestors over X-Frame-Options
# when both are present.
#
# 2026-08-28: 'self' is now the entry that matters. The Studio is EMBEDDED at
# /studio on this same origin, so the Presentation tool's preview iframe of
# /preview/* is a same-origin frame and 'self' is the whole permission it needs.
# Nothing was added here for the embedded Studio, and nothing needs to be.
#
# The *.sanity.studio and :3333/:3334 entries are LEGACY: they existed for the
# separately deployed reid-design.sanity.studio and its iframe-pane preview,
# both of which this repo stopped producing (see sanity.cli.ts). They are kept
# only until that old hosted Studio is retired in Sanity Manage, so an editor who
# still has its URL bookmarked is not left with a blank preview pane. Delete this
# line's *.sanity.studio and localhost entries at the same time as that Studio.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://reid-design.sanity.studio https://*.sanity.studio https://www.sanity.io https://*.sanity.io http://localhost:3333 http://localhost:3334
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
